#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:4
msgid "Using PkgConfig.fill_cpp_info with PKG_CONFIG_PATH from a profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:6
msgid ""
"The :ref:`PkgConfig<conan_tools_gnu_pkgconfig>` helper can read a ``.pc`` "
"file and use its contents to fill a ``cpp_info`` object with "
"``fill_cpp_info()``. When ``pkg_config_path`` is not passed explicitly, "
"``pkg-config`` locates the ``.pc`` file via the ``PKG_CONFIG_PATH`` "
"environment variable, which can be defined in the profile ``[buildenv]`` "
"section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:12
msgid ""
"A common scenario is cross-compilation with an external toolchain: the "
"toolchain provides a sysroot that already ships ``.pc`` files describing its "
"libraries (``gl.pc``, ``EGL.pc``, ``zlib.pc``, ...), and the host profile "
"points ``PKG_CONFIG_PATH`` at the sysroot's ``pkgconfig`` folder. A wrapper "
"recipe can then read those ``.pc`` files at ``package()`` time and expose "
"the information to consumers without hard-coding include and library paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:18
msgid ""
"The challenge comes when users try to define ``PKG_CONFIG_PATH`` in the "
"``[buildenv]`` section of a profile, because that is not available in the "
"``package_info()`` method of the recipes, as the package information cannot "
"rely on the \"build environment\", as the build environment is only "
"available when the package is being built, but not necessarily when the "
"package is being consumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:24
msgid ""
"The example below uses a fabricated ``mylibastral.pc`` next to the profile "
"to keep it self-contained, but the mechanism is exactly the same as pointing "
"to a real sysroot folder, to illustrate how this could be implemented if "
"necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:31
msgid ""
"This strategy is valid only for \"system\" packages, that is, recipes that "
"act as a wrapper around a system or sysroot dependency (typical in cross-"
"compilation with an external toolchain). Regular Conan packages that build "
"and package their own artifacts should not use this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:37
msgid ""
"The **profile** below adds a folder containing ``.pc`` files to "
"``PKG_CONFIG_PATH``. The ``profile_dir`` Jinja variable resolves to the "
"folder that contains the profile itself, so a ``mypcs/`` folder next to the "
"profile can be used directly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:41
msgid "*myprofile*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:41
msgid ""
"[settings]\n"
"os=Linux\n"
"arch=armv8\n"
"\n"
"[buildenv]\n"
"PKG_CONFIG_PATH+=(path){{ profile_dir }}/mypcs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:51
msgid ""
"In a real cross-compilation setup, that path would typically point to the "
"sysroot folder shipped by the toolchain, for example ``{{ sysroot }}/usr/lib/"
"pkgconfig``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:54
msgid ""
"The ``.pc`` file located in the ``mypcs`` folder besides the profile "
"describes the library (include folders, library folders, libs, defines, link "
"flags, ...):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:57
msgid "*mypcs/mylibastral.pc*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:57
msgid ""
"prefix=/usr/local\n"
"exec_prefix=${prefix}\n"
"libdir=${exec_prefix}/lib\n"
"includedir=${prefix}/include\n"
"\n"
"Name: mylibastral\n"
"Description: Interface library for Astral data flows\n"
"Version: 6.6.6\n"
"Libs: -L${libdir}/libastral -lastral -lm -Wl,--whole-archive\n"
"Cflags: -I${includedir}/libastral -D_USE_LIBASTRAL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:72
msgid ""
"The ``conanfile.py`` recipe uses ``PkgConfig`` to read ``mylibastral.pc`` "
"and populate a ``CppInfo`` object. It does it at ``package()`` time, when "
"the package is being built (the policies are added so the package is "
"automatically build when necessary in the current machine, and binaries are "
"never uploaded, as the information from that .pc file will only be valid in "
"the current machine). Notice that ``pkg_config_path`` is not passed: it is "
"picked up from ``PKG_CONFIG_PATH`` defined in the profile. The resulting "
"``CppInfo`` is serialized to the package folder in ``package()``, and "
"reloaded in ``package_info()``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:80
msgid "*conanfile.py*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:80
msgid ""
"import os\n"
"from conan import ConanFile\n"
"from conan.tools.gnu import PkgConfig\n"
"from conan.tools import CppInfo\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class Pkg(ConanFile):\n"
"    name = \"mypkg\"\n"
"    version = \"0.1\"\n"
"    build_policy = \"missing\"\n"
"    upload_policy = \"skip\"\n"
"\n"
"    def package(self):\n"
"        # This method executes at package build time, it has\n"
"        # available the build environment \"buildenv\"\n"
"        pkg_config = PkgConfig(self, \"mylibastral\")\n"
"        cpp_info = CppInfo(self)\n"
"        pkg_config.fill_cpp_info(cpp_info, is_system=False, "
"system_libs=[\"m\"])\n"
"        cpp_info.save(os.path.join(self.package_folder, \"cpp_info.json\"))\n"
"\n"
"    def package_info(self):\n"
"        # This method executes at package consumption time, it will\n"
"        # NOT have available the build environment, but it can load a file\n"
"        # generated at build/package time\n"
"        self.cpp_info = CppInfo(self).load(\"cpp_info.json\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:110
msgid "Let's now create and consume the package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:112
msgid ""
"$ conan create . -pr=myprofile\n"
"$ conan install --requires=mypkg/0.1 -pr=myprofile -g CMakeDeps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:117
msgid ""
"The generated ``mypkg-none-armv8-data.cmake`` will contain the include/lib "
"folders, libs, defines and link flags read from ``mylibastral.pc``, "
"something like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/tools/gnu/pkg_config_sysroot.rst:120
msgid ""
"set(mypkg_INCLUDE_DIRS_NONE \"/usr/local/include/libastral\")\n"
"set(mypkg_LIB_DIRS_NONE \"/usr/local/lib/libastral\")\n"
"set(mypkg_LIBS_NONE astral)\n"
"set(mypkg_SYSTEM_LIBS_NONE m)\n"
"set(mypkg_DEFINITIONS_NONE \"-D_USE_LIBASTRAL\")\n"
"set(mypkg_COMPILE_DEFINITIONS_NONE \"_USE_LIBASTRAL\")\n"
"set(mypkg_SHARED_LINK_FLAGS_NONE \"-Wl,--whole-archive\")"
msgstr ""
